<map version="1.0.1">
<node ID="ID_714" TEXT="Chapter 1 — Messages API foundations"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>2026-09-07 → 2026-09-13</p><p>Applications &amp; Integration</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_395" TEXT="🎯 Goal"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Read any Messages request or response and explain every field; build a streaming, multi-turn, multimodal chat client.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_397" TEXT="Exam domains"><node ID="ID_396" TEXT="Applications &amp; Integration — 33.1%"></node></node><node ID="ID_476" TEXT="📅 Daily plan"><node ID="ID_410" TEXT="09-07 · Python for API work: dicts/JSON, f-strings, async/await, type hints…"><node ID="ID_398" TEXT="Learn: Python for API work: dicts/JSON, f-strings, async/await, type hints, exceptions"></node><node ID="ID_403" TEXT="Build: Rewrite hello.py as a function with typed args"><node ID="ID_399" TEXT="Create ch1/client.py with def ask(prompt: str, system: str = &quot;&quot;, model: str = &quot;claude-sonnet-4-5&quot;, max_tokens: int = 512) -&gt; str."></node><node ID="ID_400" TEXT="Add an async twin using AsyncAnthropic and asyncio.gather to send three prompts concurrently; time both."></node><node ID="ID_401" TEXT="Serialise the response with r.model_dump() and print it as pretty JSON — read every key."></node><node ID="ID_402" TEXT="Wrap the call in try/except anthropic.APIError and print e.status_code and e.message."></node></node><node ID="ID_404" TEXT="✔ Done when: Sync and async versions both run; you can name every top-level key in the dumped response."></node><node ID="ID_409" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_405" TEXT="Python SDK README (sync vs async clients)" LINK="https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_406" TEXT="Library: sefoundations"></node><node ID="ID_407" TEXT="Library: requirements"></node><node ID="ID_408" TEXT="Python docs: asyncio basics, json module, dataclasses (30 min max)"></node></node></node><node ID="ID_421" TEXT="09-08 · Messages API anatomy: model, max_tokens, system, messages, roles, s…"><node ID="ID_411" TEXT="Learn: Messages API anatomy: model, max_tokens, system, messages, roles, stop_reason, usage"></node><node ID="ID_416" TEXT="Build: chat.py — multi-turn loop that keeps message history"><node ID="ID_412" TEXT="chat.py: keep a messages list; append {role:user} from input, call the API, append the assistant reply, loop."></node><node ID="ID_413" TEXT="Print stop_reason and usage after each turn; watch input_tokens grow every turn (stateless API)."></node><node ID="ID_414" TEXT="Set max_tokens=20 for one call and observe stop_reason=max_tokens and the truncated text."></node><node ID="ID_415" TEXT="Try two user messages in a row without an assistant between — read the error, then fix by merging."></node></node><node ID="ID_417" TEXT="✔ Done when: A 5-turn conversation works and you can explain why input_tokens increase each turn."></node><node ID="ID_420" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_418" TEXT="Messages API reference" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/api/messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/api/messages</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_419" TEXT="Working with messages (multi-turn, prefill)" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/working-with-messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/working-with-messages</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_431" TEXT="09-09 · Streaming: client.messages.stream, event types, text deltas, final …"><node ID="ID_422" TEXT="Learn: Streaming: client.messages.stream, event types, text deltas, final message"></node><node ID="ID_427" TEXT="Build: Add streaming to chat.py; print token by token"><node ID="ID_423" TEXT="Use with client.messages.stream(...) as s: for text in s.text_stream: print(text, end=&quot;&quot;)."></node><node ID="ID_424" TEXT="Then call s.get_final_message() and print usage — note that usage only arrives at the end."></node><node ID="ID_425" TEXT="Log the raw events once (for event in s: print(event.type)) and record the order: message_start, content_block_start, content_block_delta…, content_block_stop, message_delta, message_stop."></node><node ID="ID_426" TEXT="Handle a mid-stream error: set a tiny timeout and catch the exception cleanly."></node></node><node ID="ID_428" TEXT="✔ Done when: Streaming chat prints incrementally and still shows final usage; you can list the event sequence."></node><node ID="ID_430" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_429" TEXT="Streaming Messages" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/streaming"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/streaming</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_443" TEXT="09-10 · Structured output: JSON instructions, structured outputs (output_co…"><node ID="ID_432" TEXT="Learn: Structured output: JSON instructions, structured outputs (output_config.format / strict tools), legacy prefill and stop_sequences, validating and retrying"></node><node ID="ID_437" TEXT="Build: Script that returns validated JSON and retries on parse failure"><node ID="ID_433" TEXT="ch1/extract.py: ask Claude to extract {name, severity, component} from an incident description as JSON only."></node><node ID="ID_434" TEXT="Version A: instruction only (Sonnet 5). Version B: structured outputs — client.messages.parse(output_format=PydanticModel). Version C: a forced tool whose input_schema is the JSON shape (tool_choice type tool). Compare failure rates over 10 runs."></node><node ID="ID_435" TEXT="Version D (legacy, on Haiku 4.5 which still allows it): assistant prefill &quot;{&quot; plus stop_sequences — note that prefill is a 400 on Claude 4.6+ but still appears in exam questions."></node><node ID="ID_436" TEXT="Validate with json.loads plus a pydantic model; on failure, retry once with the error message appended; check stop_reason first (refusal / max_tokens)."></node></node><node ID="ID_438" TEXT="✔ Done when: Script returns validated JSON 10/10 times; you can rank instruction &lt; prefill (legacy) &lt; forced tool &lt; structured outputs and say why."></node><node ID="ID_442" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_439" TEXT="Structured outputs (JSON schema, strict tools)" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/structured-outputs"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/structured-outputs</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_440" TEXT="Prompting best practices (format control, prefill status)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/claude-prompting-best-practices"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/claude-prompting-best-practices</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_441" TEXT="Working with messages (prefill, roles)" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/working-with-messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/working-with-messages</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_455" TEXT="09-11 · Vision and documents: image content blocks (base64 vs URL), PDF inp…"><node ID="ID_444" TEXT="Learn: Vision and documents: image content blocks (base64 vs URL), PDF input, size limits"></node><node ID="ID_449" TEXT="Build: Send a screenshot of your dev project and ask Claude to describe it"><node ID="ID_445" TEXT="Send a PNG as {type:&quot;image&quot;, source:{type:&quot;base64&quot;, media_type:&quot;image/png&quot;, data:...}} together with a text block asking for a description."></node><node ID="ID_446" TEXT="Send the same image by URL source; note both forms."></node><node ID="ID_447" TEXT="Send a 3-page PDF as a document block and ask for a summary with page references."></node><node ID="ID_448" TEXT="Note the limits from the docs (max image size/pixels, max PDF pages) into notes/api-basics.md."></node></node><node ID="ID_450" TEXT="✔ Done when: Image (base64 and URL) and PDF requests both succeed; limits are written down."></node><node ID="ID_454" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_451" TEXT="Vision" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/vision"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/vision</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_452" TEXT="PDF support" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/pdf-support"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/pdf-support</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_453" TEXT="Files API" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/files"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/files</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_465" TEXT="09-12 · Academy: Building with the Claude API — modules 1–2 with quizzes"><node ID="ID_456" TEXT="Learn: Academy: Building with the Claude API — modules 1–2 with quizzes"></node><node ID="ID_460" TEXT="Build: Fix anything the quiz exposed"><node ID="ID_457" TEXT="Watch modules 1–2 at 1.25× speed; pause and run every code sample in your own lab instead of the notebook."></node><node ID="ID_458" TEXT="Take the module quizzes; for each wrong answer, find the sentence in the docs that settles it and paste the link into notes."></node><node ID="ID_459" TEXT="Add three questions of your own to the Self-check list below (in My notes)."></node></node><node ID="ID_461" TEXT="✔ Done when: Both module quizzes passed; every miss has a docs link in notes."></node><node ID="ID_464" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_462" TEXT="Course: Building with the Claude API" LINK="https://academy.claude.com/courses/building-with-the-claude-api"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://academy.claude.com/courses/building-with-the-claude-api</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_463" TEXT="Course: Claude Platform 101" LINK="https://academy.claude.com/courses/claude-platform-101"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://academy.claude.com/courses/claude-platform-101</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_475" TEXT="09-13 · Review day"><node ID="ID_466" TEXT="Learn: Review day"></node><node ID="ID_471" TEXT="Build: Write notes/api-basics.md"><node ID="ID_467" TEXT="Write notes/api-basics.md: request fields, response fields, stop_reason table, streaming events, content block types, prefill and stop_sequences, limits."></node><node ID="ID_468" TEXT="Do the Self-check below with answers hidden; re-read anything you got wrong."></node><node ID="ID_469" TEXT="Take the Applications &amp; Integration quiz in the Question bank tab (timed)."></node><node ID="ID_470" TEXT="Fill the Weekly retrospective for this chapter."></node></node><node ID="ID_472" TEXT="✔ Done when: Notes file committed; quiz taken and score recorded; retrospective filled."></node><node ID="ID_474" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_473" TEXT="Your own notes and the Study material section of this chapter"></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_525" TEXT="📖 Study material"><node ID="ID_489" TEXT="The request, field by field"><node ID="ID_477" TEXT="model"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>yes · Model ID. Dated IDs (claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929) are pinned; aliases (claude-sonnet-4-5) move to the latest snapshot.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_478" TEXT="max_tokens"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>yes · Hard cap on output tokens only. Hitting it sets stop_reason: max_tokens. It does not affect input.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_479" TEXT="messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>yes · Array of {role, content}. Roles alternate user/assistant; first must be user. Content is a string or a list of content blocks.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_480" TEXT="system"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · Top-level string or list of text blocks. Not a message role. Best place for role, rules, stable context (and a cache breakpoint).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_481" TEXT="temperature"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · 0–1 randomness (classic: 0 for extraction/classification, higher for creative). Does not change length or cost. Now: non-default temperature/top_p/top_k return 400 on Claude 4.7+ and were removed from the Python SDK v1 — omit them on current models.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_482" TEXT="top_p, top_k"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · Alternative sampling controls (legacy); adjust temperature or top_p, never both.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_483" TEXT="stop_sequences"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · Custom strings that end generation; sets stop_reason: stop_sequence and reports which one in stop_sequence.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_484" TEXT="stream"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · true → server-sent events.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_485" TEXT="tools, tool_choice"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · Chapter 2.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_486" TEXT="metadata.user_id"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · Opaque ID for abuse tracking; never put PII in it.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_487" TEXT="thinking"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · {type:enabled, budget_tokens} on models with manual thinking; {type:adaptive} on 4.6+ (Chapter 3).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_488" TEXT="output_config"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>no · effort (low…max) and format = {type:json_schema, schema} for structured outputs.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_494" TEXT="The response"><node ID="ID_490" TEXT="id, type: &quot;message&quot;, role: &quot;assistant&quot;, model."></node><node ID="ID_491" TEXT="content: a list of blocks — text, tool_use, thinking. Never assume content[0] is text…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>content: a list of blocks — text, tool_use, thinking. Never assume content[0] is text once tools or thinking are on.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_492" TEXT="stop_reason: end_turn (natural finish), max_tokens (truncated), stop_sequence (hit…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>stop_reason: end_turn (natural finish), max_tokens (truncated), stop_sequence (hit your string), tool_use (wants a tool), refusal (safety classifier — still HTTP 200), pause_turn (long server-tool turns — send it back to continue), model_context_window_exceeded (input + max_tokens over the window).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_493" TEXT="usage: input_tokens, output_tokens, and with caching cache_creation_input_tokens,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>usage: input_tokens, output_tokens, and with caching cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens. This is how you cost a call.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_497" TEXT="Statelessness and conversation history"><node ID="ID_495" TEXT="The API keeps nothing between calls. Every request carries the whole history, so input…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>The API keeps nothing between calls. Every request carries the whole history, so input tokens grow every turn — the reason context management (Chapter 3) and caching (Chapter 2) exist.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_496" TEXT="Consecutive same-role messages are an error on most models; merge them into one…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Consecutive same-role messages are an error on most models; merge them into one message with several content blocks.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_502" TEXT="Streaming"><node ID="ID_498" TEXT="Event order: message_start → (content_block_start → content_block_delta* →…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Event order: message_start → (content_block_start → content_block_delta* → content_block_stop)* → message_delta (carries stop_reason and output usage) → message_stop.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_499" TEXT="Delta types: text_delta, input_json_delta (tool arguments arrive as partial JSON),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Delta types: text_delta, input_json_delta (tool arguments arrive as partial JSON), thinking_delta.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_500" TEXT="Streaming improves perceived latency and lets you show progress; it does not change…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Streaming improves perceived latency and lets you show progress; it does not change cost or total time. Use it for anything user-facing; also recommended for long outputs to avoid HTTP timeouts.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_501" TEXT="The SDK helper messages.stream() accumulates the final message for you; the raw…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>The SDK helper messages.stream() accumulates the final message for you; the raw stream=True form gives you events.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_509" TEXT="Controlling the output shape"><node ID="ID_503" TEXT="Instruction in system: &quot;Respond only with JSON matching…&quot;. Cheap, not guaranteed."></node><node ID="ID_504" TEXT="Prefill (legacy): put a partial assistant message last (e.g. { or &lt;answer&gt;) — Claude…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Prefill (legacy): put a partial assistant message last (e.g. { or &lt;answer&gt;) — Claude continues from it; removes preambles. Never worked with extended thinking, and is a 400 error on Claude 4.6+. The exam may still present it as a valid technique — know how it worked.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_505" TEXT="stop_sequences: stop at &lt;/answer&gt; or a closing brace to avoid trailing chatter."></node><node ID="ID_506" TEXT="Tool use as a schema: define a tool whose input_schema is your desired JSON and force…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Tool use as a schema: define a tool whose input_schema is your desired JSON and force it with tool_choice — the classic guaranteed-structure trick.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_507" TEXT="Structured outputs: output_config.format = {type:&quot;json_schema&quot;, schema} (or strict:…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Structured outputs: output_config.format = {type:&quot;json_schema&quot;, schema} (or strict: true on a tool) constrains generation to the schema — GA on Sonnet 4.5+/Opus 4.5+/Haiku 4.5. Output can still be off-schema when stop_reason is refusal or max_tokens, so check stop_reason first.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_508" TEXT="Always validate and retry anyway; treat model output as untrusted input."></node></node><node ID="ID_520" TEXT="Vision and documents"><node ID="ID_510" TEXT="Images are content blocks: {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;base64&quot;|&quot;url&quot;, ...}}.…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Images are content blocks: {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;base64&quot;|&quot;url&quot;, ...}}. Formats JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP; several images per request; put images before the question text.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_511" TEXT="PDFs go in as document blocks (base64, URL or file_id via the Files API); Claude sees…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>PDFs go in as document blocks (base64, URL or file_id via the Files API); Claude sees both extracted text and page images, so tables and charts work. Page limits exist — check the docs for your model.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_512" TEXT="Image tokens ≈ ceil(width/28) × ceil(height/28) (older docs said width×height/750 —…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Image tokens ≈ ceil(width/28) × ceil(height/28) (older docs said width×height/750 — same order of magnitude: a 1000×1000 image ≈ 1,300 tokens). Max 10 MB (5 MB on Bedrock/Vertex), auto-downscaled to a 1568 px long edge; resize before sending.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_519" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_513" TEXT="&quot;Which parameter controls response length?&quot; → max_tokens, not temperature."></node><node ID="ID_514" TEXT="&quot;Why did the answer cut off mid-sentence?&quot; → stop_reason=max_tokens."></node><node ID="ID_515" TEXT="System prompt is not a message."></node><node ID="ID_516" TEXT="Streaming does not reduce cost."></node><node ID="ID_517" TEXT="Prefill goes in the assistant role, as the last message (legacy on 4.6+). content is a list, not a string."></node><node ID="ID_518" TEXT="A refusal is HTTP 200 with stop_reason refusal."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_522" TEXT="Minimal call"><node ID="ID_521" TEXT="{ } code sample"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>from anthropic import Anthropic</p><p>client = Anthropic()          # reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</p><p>r = client.messages.create(</p><p>    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;,</p><p>    max_tokens=512,</p><p>    system=&quot;You are a concise DevOps assistant.&quot;,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;Explain a Kubernetes liveness probe in 2 lines.&quot;}],</p><p>)</p><p>print(r.content[0].text, r.stop_reason, r.usage)</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_524" TEXT="Streaming with the SDK helper"><node ID="ID_523" TEXT="{ } code sample"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>with client.messages.stream(model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=800,</p><p>        messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;Write a haiku about Terraform state.&quot;}]) as s:</p><p>    for text in s.text_stream:</p><p>        print(text, end=&quot;&quot;, flush=True)</p><p>final = s.get_final_message()</p><p>print(&quot;\n&quot;, final.stop_reason, final.usage.output_tokens)</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_664" TEXT="📚 Library digests"><node ID="ID_542" TEXT="Messages API reference" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/messages</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_536" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_526" TEXT="POST /v1/messages. Required: model, messages (array of {role, content}; role ∈ user |…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>POST /v1/messages. Required: model, messages (array of {role, content}; role ∈ user | assistant), max_tokens. Optional: system, stop_sequences, metadata.user_id (≤512 chars, opaque — no identifying info), tools, tool_choice, thinking, output_config, container.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_527" TEXT="tool_choice types: auto (default), any (must call some tool), tool + name (must call that tool),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>tool_choice types: auto (default), any (must call some tool), tool + name (must call that tool), none. auto/any/tool accept disable_parallel_tool_use.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_528" TEXT="thinking: {type:'enabled', budget_tokens ≥ 1024 and &lt; max_tokens} on models that support manual…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>thinking: {type:'enabled', budget_tokens ≥ 1024 and &lt; max_tokens} on models that support manual thinking; {type:'adaptive'} on Claude 4.6+; {type:'disabled'}. output_config: effort ∈ low | medium | high | xhigh | max; format = {type:'json_schema', schema}.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_529" TEXT="cache_control: {type:'ephemeral', ttl?: '5m' | '1h'} — allowed on text, image, document,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>cache_control: {type:'ephemeral', ttl?: '5m' | '1h'} — allowed on text, image, document, tool_use, tool_result blocks and on tool definitions.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_530" TEXT="Content sources: base64 (image media_type jpeg/png/gif/webp; PDF application/pdf), url, file…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Content sources: base64 (image media_type jpeg/png/gif/webp; PDF application/pdf), url, file (file_id from the Files API), text (text/plain documents).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_531" TEXT="Response: id, type 'message', role 'assistant', content[] (blocks: text, thinking,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Response: id, type 'message', role 'assistant', content[] (blocks: text, thinking, redacted_thinking, tool_use, server_tool_use, web_search_result…), model, stop_reason, stop_sequence (null unless hit), usage.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_532" TEXT="stop_reason enum: end_turn, max_tokens, stop_sequence, tool_use, pause_turn, refusal,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>stop_reason enum: end_turn, max_tokens, stop_sequence, tool_use, pause_turn, refusal, model_context_window_exceeded. A refusal carries stop_details with a category.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_533" TEXT="usage: input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>usage: input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens, cache_creation.{ephemeral_5m_input_tokens, ephemeral_1h_input_tokens}, server_tool_use.{web_search_requests, web_fetch_requests}, output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_534" TEXT="Tool names must match ^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,256}$; server-tool ids start srvtoolu_. Citations are off…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Tool names must match ^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,256}$; server-tool ids start srvtoolu_. Citations are off by default (citations: {enabled:false}).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_535" TEXT="Related endpoints: POST /v1/messages/count_tokens; /v1/messages/batches (create, list, get,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Related endpoints: POST /v1/messages/count_tokens; /v1/messages/batches (create, list, get, cancel, delete, results).</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_540" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_537" TEXT="max_tokens is required and has no default; system is a top-level field, never a message with role 'system' at index 0."></node><node ID="ID_538" TEXT="budget_tokens must be ≥1024 and &lt; max_tokens; tool_choice 'any' forces some tool, 'tool' forces a named one."></node><node ID="ID_539" TEXT="stop_sequence is populated only when stop_reason == 'stop_sequence'; cache_read_input_tokens is reported separately from input_tokens."></node></node><node ID="ID_541" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>import anthropic</p><p>client = anthropic.Anthropic()          # reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</p><p>msg = client.messages.create(</p><p>    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    system=&quot;You are terse.&quot;,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello, Claude&quot;}],</p><p>    metadata={&quot;user_id&quot;: &quot;hashed-user-123&quot;},</p><p>)</p><p>print(msg.stop_reason, msg.usage.input_tokens, msg.content[0].text)</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_557" TEXT="Working with messages (multi-turn, roles, prefill)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/working-with-messages"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/working-with-messages</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_550" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_543" TEXT="The API is stateless — send the full conversation history on every call."></node><node ID="ID_544" TEXT="Messages alternate user/assistant; consecutive same-role messages are combined into one turn.…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Messages alternate user/assistant; consecutive same-role messages are combined into one turn. The first message must be user.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_545" TEXT="A role 'system' message may appear mid-conversation on the newest models (4.8+, Opus 5, Fable 5)…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>A role 'system' message may appear mid-conversation on the newest models (4.8+, Opus 5, Fable 5) but never first; use top-level system for from-the-start instructions. Mid-conversation system turns don't invalidate the cached prefix.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_546" TEXT="Prefill (a partial assistant message as the final turn, e.g. '{' or 'The answer is (') is NOT…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Prefill (a partial assistant message as the final turn, e.g. '{' or 'The answer is (') is NOT supported on Claude 4.6 and later — use structured outputs or explicit format instructions. Older models still accept it.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_547" TEXT="temperature, top_p, top_k return HTTP 400 on Claude 4.7+ when set to non-default values; omit…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>temperature, top_p, top_k return HTTP 400 on Claude 4.7+ when set to non-default values; omit them. (Python SDK v1.0+ removed the parameters.)</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_548" TEXT="You may inject synthetic assistant turns to shape the flow of a conversation."></node><node ID="ID_549" TEXT="Image sources: base64, url, file; formats jpeg/png/gif/webp."></node></node><node ID="ID_554" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_551" TEXT="First message role must be user."></node><node ID="ID_552" TEXT="Prefilling the assistant turn is legacy: on 4.6+ it is a 400 error and the replacement is output_config.format (structured outputs)."></node><node ID="ID_553" TEXT="Sampling parameters (temperature/top_p/top_k) are rejected on 4.7+, not silently ignored."></node></node><node ID="ID_555" TEXT="Then vs now"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>The exam blueprint predates these changes, so a question may still present prefill or temperature as valid techniques. Answer such questions with the classic behaviour (prefill forces format; temperature controls randomness) unless the stem names a Claude 4.6+/4.7+ model.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_556" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>msg = client.messages.create(</p><p>    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    messages=[</p><p>        {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello, Claude&quot;},</p><p>        {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;assistant&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello!&quot;},</p><p>        {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Can you describe LLMs?&quot;},</p><p>    ])</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_571" TEXT="Streaming Messages" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_565" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_558" TEXT="Set stream: true; transport is server-sent events (SSE)."></node><node ID="ID_559" TEXT="Event order: message_start → (content_block_start → content_block_delta* → content_block_stop)*…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Event order: message_start → (content_block_start → content_block_delta* → content_block_stop)* → message_delta → message_stop. ping can appear anywhere; an error event (e.g. overloaded_error) can arrive mid-stream after a 200.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_560" TEXT="Delta types: text_delta (text), input_json_delta (partial_json — accumulate then parse),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Delta types: text_delta (text), input_json_delta (partial_json — accumulate then parse), thinking_delta, signature_delta (just before a thinking block stops), citations_delta.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_561" TEXT="message_start usage shows input_tokens (and output_tokens: 1); message_delta carries cumulative…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>message_start usage shows input_tokens (and output_tokens: 1); message_delta carries cumulative output usage and the stop_reason.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_562" TEXT="Streaming is required when max_tokens exceeds 128,000; non-streaming requests time out at about…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Streaming is required when max_tokens exceeds 128,000; non-streaming requests time out at about 10 minutes.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_563" TEXT="Python helpers: client.messages.stream() context manager, .text_stream, .get_final_message().…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Python helpers: client.messages.stream() context manager, .text_stream, .get_final_message(). TS: .finalMessage().</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_564" TEXT="Recovering an interrupted stream: on 4.6+ send a user message 'Your previous response was…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Recovering an interrupted stream: on 4.6+ send a user message 'Your previous response was interrupted and ended with […]. Continue from where you left off.' Tool-use and thinking blocks cannot be partially recovered — resume from the last text block.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_569" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_566" TEXT="Tool inputs arrive as input_json_delta.partial_json strings that must be concatenated — never as complete objects."></node><node ID="ID_567" TEXT="Final usage and stop_reason come in message_delta, not message_stop."></node><node ID="ID_568" TEXT="An SSE error event can arrive after HTTP 200 — handle overloaded_error inside the stream."></node></node><node ID="ID_570" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>with client.messages.stream(</p><p>    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello&quot;}],</p><p>) as stream:</p><p>    for text in stream.text_stream:</p><p>        print(text, end=&quot;&quot;, flush=True)</p><p>final = stream.get_final_message()</p><p>print(final.stop_reason, final.usage.output_tokens)</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_588" TEXT="Structured outputs (JSON schema + strict tools)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_581" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_572" TEXT="Two features: JSON outputs via output_config.format = {type:'json_schema', schema} (replaces the…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Two features: JSON outputs via output_config.format = {type:'json_schema', schema} (replaces the deprecated output_format name), and strict tool use via strict: true on a tool definition. GA — no beta header needed.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_573" TEXT="Supported: Opus 4.5+, Sonnet 4.5+, Haiku 4.5, Fable/Mythos 5.x."></node><node ID="ID_574" TEXT="Schema support: standard types, enum, const, required, anyOf, type arrays (['string','null']),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Schema support: standard types, enum, const, required, anyOf, type arrays (['string','null']), nested objects/arrays, additionalProperties:false (required — SDK adds it), limited format/pattern. Not supported: minimum/maximum, minLength/maxLength, minItems/maxItems, not, allOf, most oneOf, $ref, if/then/else — the SDK strips them and appends the constraint to descriptions.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_575" TEXT="Limits: 20 strict tools per request; 24 optional parameters combined; 16 union-type parameters;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Limits: 20 strict tools per request; 24 optional parameters combined; 16 union-type parameters; 180 s grammar compile timeout. Grammar is cached 24 h; invalidated by schema structure or tool-set changes, not by name/description edits.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_576" TEXT="Changing output_config.format invalidates the prompt cache; a small input-token overhead is…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Changing output_config.format invalidates the prompt cache; a small input-token overhead is added by an injected system prompt.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_577" TEXT="Output may NOT match the schema when stop_reason is refusal (still HTTP 200, still billed) or…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Output may NOT match the schema when stop_reason is refusal (still HTTP 200, still billed) or max_tokens — always check stop_reason before parsing.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_578" TEXT="Enum casing may drift — compare case-insensitively; required properties are emitted before…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Enum casing may drift — compare case-insensitively; required properties are emitted before optional ones.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_579" TEXT="Incompatible with citations (400) and with prefill; the grammar constrains only the final…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Incompatible with citations (400) and with prefill; the grammar constrains only the final output, not tool calls or thinking. Works with streaming, Batches (50% off) and token counting.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_580" TEXT="Python SDK: client.messages.parse(output_format=PydanticModel) → response.parsed_output;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Python SDK: client.messages.parse(output_format=PydanticModel) → response.parsed_output; anthropic.transform_schema() helper.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_585" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_582" TEXT="The raw API parameter is output_config.format — not response_format, not top-level output_format."></node><node ID="ID_583" TEXT="Structured output + citations → 400."></node><node ID="ID_584" TEXT="stop_reason 'refusal' returns HTTP 200 with non-conforming output — check stop_reason, don't just json.loads."></node></node><node ID="ID_586" TEXT="Then vs now"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Classic exam answers for 'guaranteed JSON' were prefill + validation, or a forced tool with input_schema. Both still count as correct reasoning; structured outputs is the modern, stronger answer where the options include it.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_587" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>from pydantic import BaseModel</p><p>class Incident(BaseModel):</p><p>    name: str</p><p>    severity: str</p><p>    component: str</p><p>resp = client.messages.parse(</p><p>    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=512,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: incident_text}],</p><p>    output_format=Incident,</p><p>)</p><p>print(resp.parsed_output)   # validated Incident instance</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_601" TEXT="Vision (images)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/vision"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/vision</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_595" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_589" TEXT="Formats: image/jpeg, image/png, image/gif (first frame only), image/webp. Sources: base64, url,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Formats: image/jpeg, image/png, image/gif (first frame only), image/webp. Sources: base64, url, file (Files API — recommended when reusing an image across turns).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_590" TEXT="Max size 10 MB base64 on the Claude API (5 MB on Bedrock/Vertex); max 8000×8000 px; with more…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Max size 10 MB base64 on the Claude API (5 MB on Bedrock/Vertex); max 8000×8000 px; with more than 20 images per request each is capped at 2000×2000.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_591" TEXT="Auto-downscaled preserving aspect ratio to a long edge of 1568 px (standard) or 2576 px…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Auto-downscaled preserving aspect ratio to a long edge of 1568 px (standard) or 2576 px (high-res, Claude 4.7+). 'oversized_image': 'error' rejects instead of resizing.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_592" TEXT="Per request: 100 images on 200K-context models, 600 on 1M models; claude.ai 20 per message."></node><node ID="ID_593" TEXT="Token cost ≈ ceil(width/28) × ceil(height/28): 200×200 = 64 tokens; 1000×1000 ≈ 1,296; 1920×1080…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Token cost ≈ ceil(width/28) × ceil(height/28): 200×200 = 64 tokens; 1000×1000 ≈ 1,296; 1920×1080 ≈ 1,560 (standard). Example: Haiku 4.5 at $1/MTok → about $1.30 per 1,000 1000×1000 images.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_594" TEXT="Limitations: cannot identify people; weak on &lt;200 px, rotated or low-quality images; approximate…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Limitations: cannot identify people; weak on &lt;200 px, rotated or low-quality images; approximate spatial coordinates; poor at counting many small objects; cannot detect AI-generated images; not for medical scans; no image generation.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_599" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_596" TEXT="The token formula is now width/28 × height/28 (28-px patches); the old (w×h)/750 rule is out of date — both give the same order of magnitude."></node><node ID="ID_597" TEXT="Bedrock/Vertex cap images at 5 MB vs 10 MB on the Claude API."></node><node ID="ID_598" TEXT="More than 20 images in a request lowers the per-image cap to 2000×2000."></node></node><node ID="ID_600" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>import base64</p><p>data = base64.standard_b64encode(open(&quot;shot.png&quot;,&quot;rb&quot;).read()).decode()</p><p>msg = client.messages.create(model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;base64&quot;,&quot;media_type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;data&quot;:data}},</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Describe this screenshot.&quot;}]}])</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_613" TEXT="PDF support (document blocks)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/pdf-support"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/pdf-support</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_607" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_602" TEXT="Content block type 'document', media_type application/pdf; sources url, base64, file (file_id).…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Content block type 'document', media_type application/pdf; sources url, base64, file (file_id). Plain text (.txt/.csv/.md) uses text/plain; .docx/.xlsx must be converted first.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_603" TEXT="Limits: 32 MB per request; 600 pages (100 pages on models with a 200K window); no…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Limits: 32 MB per request; 600 pages (100 pages on models with a 200K window); no encrypted/password PDFs.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_604" TEXT="Each page is rasterised to an image AND its text extracted; both go to the model (so charts and…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Each page is rasterised to an image AND its text extracted; both go to the model (so charts and tables work). Cost = 1,500–3,000 text tokens per page plus image tokens; no extra PDF fee.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_605" TEXT="Put document blocks before the text in the user message; refer to logical page numbers; split…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Put document blocks before the text in the user message; refer to logical page numbers; split very large PDFs.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_606" TEXT="Supports cache_control on the document block, citations, and Message Batches."></node></node><node ID="ID_611" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_608" TEXT="600 pages on 1M-context models but only 100 on 200K models such as Haiku 4.5."></node><node ID="ID_609" TEXT="PDFs are billed as text AND image tokens per page."></node><node ID="ID_610" TEXT="Block type is 'document', not 'image'."></node></node><node ID="ID_612" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>msg = client.messages.create(model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;document&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;url&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://example.com/report.pdf&quot;},</p><p>         &quot;cache_control&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;ephemeral&quot;}},</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;What are the key findings? Cite pages.&quot;}]}])</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_626" TEXT="Files API" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/files"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/files</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_620" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_614" TEXT="GA. Endpoints: POST /v1/files (upload), GET /v1/files, GET /v1/files/{id}, GET…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>GA. Endpoints: POST /v1/files (upload), GET /v1/files, GET /v1/files/{id}, GET /v1/files/{id}/content, DELETE /v1/files/{id}.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_615" TEXT="Limits: 500 MB per file, 1 TB per organisation, ~500 requests/min."></node><node ID="ID_616" TEXT="Mapping: PDF → document; text/plain → document; jpeg/png/gif/webp → image; other files →…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Mapping: PDF → document; text/plain → document; jpeg/png/gif/webp → image; other files → container_upload (for code execution).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_617" TEXT="Reference with source {type:'file', file_id}. Uploaded files are not downloadable (400) — only…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Reference with source {type:'file', file_id}. Uploaded files are not downloadable (400) — only files produced by code execution/skills are.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_618" TEXT="Optional expires_in_seconds at upload: 1 hour to 90 days. Files are workspace-scoped — any key…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Optional expires_in_seconds at upload: 1 hour to 90 days. Files are workspace-scoped — any key in the workspace can read them; never accept file_ids from untrusted users; use one workspace per tenant.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_619" TEXT="Upload/storage is free; content is billed as input tokens every time it is referenced. Not…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Upload/storage is free; content is billed as input tokens every time it is referenced. Not ZDR-eligible.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_624" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_621" TEXT="Files are workspace-scoped, not per key or per user."></node><node ID="ID_622" TEXT="Uploading is free; you pay tokens each time the file is used in a request."></node><node ID="ID_623" TEXT="You cannot download a file you uploaded — only tool-generated outputs."></node></node><node ID="ID_625" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>up = client.files.upload(file=(&quot;doc.pdf&quot;, open(&quot;doc.pdf&quot;,&quot;rb&quot;), &quot;application/pdf&quot;))</p><p>msg = client.messages.create(model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=1024,</p><p>    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;document&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;file&quot;,&quot;file_id&quot;:up.id}},</p><p>        {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Summarise this.&quot;}]}])</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_639" TEXT="Client SDKs (Python)" LINK="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/sdks/python"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/sdks/python</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_633" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_627" TEXT="Official SDKs: Python, TypeScript, C#, Go, Java, PHP, Ruby (+ CLI, Swift, OpenAI-compat layer).…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Official SDKs: Python, TypeScript, C#, Go, Java, PHP, Ruby (+ CLI, Swift, OpenAI-compat layer). Python: pip install anthropic, Python ≥3.10, reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_628" TEXT="Clients: Anthropic, AsyncAnthropic, AnthropicBedrock, AnthropicVertex, AnthropicFoundry (and AWS…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Clients: Anthropic, AsyncAnthropic, AnthropicBedrock, AnthropicVertex, AnthropicFoundry (and AWS variants).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_629" TEXT="Defaults: max_retries=2 (exponential backoff, honours retry-after); timeout 10 minutes. Retried…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Defaults: max_retries=2 (exponential backoff, honours retry-after); timeout 10 minutes. Retried automatically: connection errors, 408, 409, 429, ≥500. Per-call override: client.with_options(max_retries=5, timeout=20.0).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_630" TEXT="Exceptions: APIStatusError base → BadRequestError 400, AuthenticationError 401,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Exceptions: APIStatusError base → BadRequestError 400, AuthenticationError 401, PermissionDeniedError 403, NotFoundError 404, ConflictError 409, UnprocessableEntityError 422, RateLimitError 429, InternalServerError ≥500; plus APIConnectionError, APITimeoutError.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_631" TEXT="Helpers: messages.stream(), messages.parse(), messages.count_tokens(), files.upload(),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Helpers: messages.stream(), messages.parse(), messages.count_tokens(), files.upload(), client.beta.messages with betas=[...], auto-pagination on .list(), message.to_dict(), message._request_id.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_632" TEXT="SDK v1.0+ removed temperature/top_p/top_k (TypeError if passed)."></node></node><node ID="ID_637" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_634" TEXT="Default retries = 2 (three attempts total); default timeout = 10 minutes."></node><node ID="ID_635" TEXT="Beta features go through client.beta.messages with a betas=[...] list."></node><node ID="ID_636" TEXT="429 and 5xx are auto-retried; 400/401/403/404 are not."></node></node><node ID="ID_638" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>from anthropic import Anthropic, RateLimitError, APIStatusError</p><p>client = Anthropic(max_retries=3, timeout=60)</p><p>try:</p><p>    m = client.with_options(timeout=20.0).messages.create(</p><p>        model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;, max_tokens=256,</p><p>        messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;ping&quot;}])</p><p>    print(m._request_id)</p><p>except RateLimitError as e:</p><p>    print(&quot;429&quot;, e.response.headers.get(&quot;retry-after&quot;))</p><p>except APIStatusError as e:</p><p>    print(e.status_code, e.message)</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_652" TEXT="Software engineering foundations for Claude apps (REST, JSON, git, refactoring) — blueprint 7.4%"><node ID="ID_646" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_640" TEXT="REST essentials the API relies on: HTTPS POST /v1/messages with headers x-api-key,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>REST essentials the API relies on: HTTPS POST /v1/messages with headers x-api-key, anthropic-version (e.g. 2023-06-01), content-type: application/json; status classes 2xx success / 4xx client / 5xx server; idempotency matters for retries (a retried POST can double-charge — make your own writes idempotent).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_641" TEXT="JSON discipline: content is a list of typed blocks, not a string; parse with a strict parser,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>JSON discipline: content is a list of typed blocks, not a string; parse with a strict parser, validate with a schema (pydantic / zod), never eval; handle unicode, escaping and large numbers; treat model output as untrusted input.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_642" TEXT="Version control: keep prompts, tool schemas, CLAUDE.md, settings.json and eval cases in the…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Version control: keep prompts, tool schemas, CLAUDE.md, settings.json and eval cases in the repo; pin model IDs and SDK versions (requirements.txt / package-lock); tag releases; never commit .env or keys (.gitignore, secret scanning); review prompt changes like code changes (diff + eval run).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_643" TEXT="Refactoring for LLM code: isolate the API call behind one function (client, model, retries,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Refactoring for LLM code: isolate the API call behind one function (client, model, retries, logging in one place); separate prompt templates from code; make tools small pure functions with typed inputs; add tests around parsing and tool handlers; remove dead prompt text — every token costs.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_644" TEXT="Async and concurrency: use the async client with bounded concurrency (semaphore) to respect rate…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Async and concurrency: use the async client with bounded concurrency (semaphore) to respect rate limits; stream for user-facing paths; batch for offline paths.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_645" TEXT="Observability: log request id, model, stop_reason, usage, latency, tool calls; emit metrics…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Observability: log request id, model, stop_reason, usage, latency, tool calls; emit metrics (cost per request, cache hit rate, refusal rate, p95 latency); keep traces for debugging.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_650" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_647" TEXT="A retried POST is not automatically safe — make downstream writes idempotent."></node><node ID="ID_648" TEXT="Pin model IDs and SDK versions in version control; treat prompt edits like code (review + eval)."></node><node ID="ID_649" TEXT="Model output is untrusted input — schema-validate before use."></node></node><node ID="ID_651" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>import asyncio</p><p>from anthropic import AsyncAnthropic</p><p>client = AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=3)</p><p>sem = asyncio.Semaphore(8)                 # bounded concurrency vs rate limits</p><p>async def ask(prompt):</p><p>    async with sem:</p><p>        r = await client.messages.create(model=&quot;claude-haiku-4-5-20251001&quot;, max_tokens=200,</p><p>            messages=[{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:prompt}])</p><p>        return r.content[0].text, r.usage</p><p>results = asyncio.run(asyncio.gather(*(ask(p) for p in prompts)))</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_663" TEXT="Understanding requirements and the systems life cycle — blueprint 6.2%"><node ID="ID_658" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_653" TEXT="Requirements for an LLM feature: user goal and success criteria (measurable, see evals); input…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Requirements for an LLM feature: user goal and success criteria (measurable, see evals); input types (text, images, PDFs, tool data); latency budget (interactive → stream, small model; batch → Batches); cost ceiling per request/month; quality bar and failure tolerance; privacy/PII constraints and data residency; safety/compliance domain (high-risk → human oversight); who is accountable for outputs.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_654" TEXT="Decide the architecture from the requirements: single prompt → workflow → agent, in that order;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Decide the architecture from the requirements: single prompt → workflow → agent, in that order; choose the smallest model that meets the bar; decide state handling (stateless request, server-side session store, retrieval).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_655" TEXT="Life cycle: define criteria → prototype in the Workbench → build eval set → implement with…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Life cycle: define criteria → prototype in the Workbench → build eval set → implement with logging → red-team → staged rollout (shadow / canary / percentage) → monitor (quality, cost, latency, refusals, injection attempts) → iterate on prompt/model with regression evals → plan for model deprecations (60-day notice) and version pinning.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_656" TEXT="Operational readiness: rate-limit headroom and backoff, spend limits per workspace, secrets…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Operational readiness: rate-limit headroom and backoff, spend limits per workspace, secrets rotation, fallbacks when 529/overloaded (degrade to smaller model or queue), runbooks for tool failures.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_657" TEXT="Change management: every prompt/model/tool change goes through the eval suite and a diff review;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Change management: every prompt/model/tool change goes through the eval suite and a diff review; keep a changelog of prompt versions with their eval scores.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_662" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_659" TEXT="The first design question is 'what does success look like and how will we measure it?', not 'which model?'."></node><node ID="ID_660" TEXT="Interactive latency requirement rules out Batches; cost requirement pushes toward caching and Haiku."></node><node ID="ID_661" TEXT="Plan for deprecation from day one: pin IDs, keep evals ready to validate the successor model."></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_685" TEXT="❓ Self-check"><node ID="ID_666" TEXT="A response ends with stop_reason = max_tokens. What happened and what do you do?"><node ID="ID_665" TEXT="→ Output hit the cap. Raise max_tokens or ask for a shorter answer; optionally send a follow-up 'continue' with the partial text as the assistant turn."></node></node><node ID="ID_668" TEXT="Where does the system prompt go in a Messages request?"><node ID="ID_667" TEXT="→ In the top-level system parameter, not inside messages."></node></node><node ID="ID_670" TEXT="How do you force JSON output without a schema feature?"><node ID="ID_669" TEXT="→ Prefill the assistant turn with '{', instruct JSON-only in system, validate and retry on failure — or define a tool with the schema and force it via tool_choice."></node></node><node ID="ID_672" TEXT="Why do input_tokens grow on every turn of a chat?"><node ID="ID_671" TEXT="→ The API is stateless; you resend the whole history each call."></node></node><node ID="ID_674" TEXT="Name the streaming events in order."><node ID="ID_673" TEXT="→ message_start, content_block_start, content_block_delta (repeated), content_block_stop, message_delta, message_stop."></node></node><node ID="ID_676" TEXT="When does usage arrive in a streamed response?"><node ID="ID_675" TEXT="→ Input tokens in message_start; output tokens in message_delta near the end — so cost is only known at the end."></node></node><node ID="ID_678" TEXT="Two user messages in a row — what happens?"><node ID="ID_677" TEXT="→ Error on most models (roles must alternate). Merge into one user message with multiple content blocks."></node></node><node ID="ID_680" TEXT="A user sends a 12 MB PNG. What should your app do?"><node ID="ID_679" TEXT="→ Resize/compress before sending — image cost scales with pixel area and there is a size cap."></node></node><node ID="ID_682" TEXT="What does temperature=0 buy you?"><node ID="ID_681" TEXT="→ Near-deterministic, most-likely output — good for extraction and classification. It does not shorten the answer."></node></node><node ID="ID_684" TEXT="Which response field tells you a tool call is requested?"><node ID="ID_683" TEXT="→ stop_reason = tool_use, with a tool_use block in content."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_698" TEXT="⚠ Traps to drill"><node ID="ID_687" TEXT="Answer cut off mid-sentence."><node ID="ID_686" TEXT="→ stop_reason=max_tokens — raise max_tokens; temperature has nothing to do with length."></node></node><node ID="ID_689" TEXT="Where is the system prompt sent?"><node ID="ID_688" TEXT="→ Top-level system parameter — never as a message with role 'system'."></node></node><node ID="ID_691" TEXT="Does streaming reduce cost or total latency?"><node ID="ID_690" TEXT="→ No. It improves perceived latency only; tokens billed are identical."></node></node><node ID="ID_693" TEXT="Prefill lives in which role and position?"><node ID="ID_692" TEXT="→ Assistant role, as the final message; Claude continues from it (legacy — 400 on Claude 4.6+; use structured outputs)."></node></node><node ID="ID_695" TEXT="response.content is a string?"><node ID="ID_694" TEXT="→ No — a list of blocks (text, tool_use, thinking). Iterate, don't index blindly."></node></node><node ID="ID_697" TEXT="Which parameter is required besides model and messages?"><node ID="ID_696" TEXT="→ max_tokens."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_706" TEXT="🗒 Cheat sheet"><node ID="ID_699" TEXT="Required: model, max_tokens, messages. system is top-level. Roles alternate, first is user."></node><node ID="ID_700" TEXT="stop_reason: end_turn · max_tokens (truncated) · stop_sequence · tool_use · refusal (HTTP 200) · pause_turn (send back) · model_context_window_exceeded"></node><node ID="ID_701" TEXT="usage: input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens"></node><node ID="ID_702" TEXT="Stream events: message_start → content_block_start/delta/stop → message_delta (stop_reason, output usage) → message_stop"></node><node ID="ID_703" TEXT="Force shape: instruction &lt; prefill '{' + stop_sequences (legacy, 400 on 4.6+) &lt; forced tool with input_schema &lt; structured outputs output_config.format (check stop_reason before parsing)"></node><node ID="ID_704" TEXT="Images: base64/URL/file blocks, JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP, ≤10 MB, tokens ≈ (w/28)×(h/28); PDFs as document blocks (text + page images), 32 MB, 600 pages (100 on 200K models)"></node><node ID="ID_705" TEXT="Stateless API: resend full history each call → context grows → cache the prefix, summarise old turns"></node></node><node ID="ID_713" TEXT="☑ Chapter checklist"><node ID="ID_707" TEXT="Can explain every field in a Messages request and response from memory"></node><node ID="ID_708" TEXT="Know the difference between stop_reason values: end_turn, max_tokens, stop_sequence, tool_use (and refusal / pause_turn where they apply)"></node><node ID="ID_709" TEXT="Streaming chat works and handles the final message event"></node><node ID="ID_710" TEXT="JSON-output script validates and retries"></node><node ID="ID_711" TEXT="Sent an image and a PDF successfully"></node><node ID="ID_712" TEXT="notes/api-basics.md written"></node></node></node>
</map>
